039|2024-01-19|confirmed spam|\r\n|5030|2024-01-18|spam content|\r\n|5002|2024-01-15|violence violation|\r\n|5037|2024-01-19|inappropriate material|\r\n|5013|2024-01-16|spam advertisement|\r\n|5011|2024-01-16|inappropriate content|\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n**Requirements**\r\n\r\n- Only consider rows where `action` is \"report\" from user_actions\r\n- Count unique reported posts per day (multiple reports of the same post count once)\r\n- Count only posts removed on the same day they were reported\r\n- If a day has reported posts but no removals, show 0 removed posts and a 0 ratio\r\n- Round removal_ratio to 2 decimal places\r\n- Output one row per date that has reported posts\r\n- Use the provided DataFrames as-is, do not modify or reconstruct the datasets\r\n\r\n**Returns**\r\n\r\n- `pandas.DataFrame` with columns: `date`, `reported_posts`, `removed_posts`, `removal_ratio`\r\n\r\n**Expected Output**\r\n\r\n| date       | reported\\_posts | removed\\_posts | removal_ratio |\r\n| ---------- | -------------- | ------------- | ------------- |\r\n| 2024-01-15 | 5              | 2             | 0.40          |\r\n| 2024-01-16 | 6              | 2             | 0.33          |\r\n| 2024-01-18 | 8              | 2             | 0.25          |\r\n| 2024-01-19 | 9              | 2             | 0.22          |",
  "short_text": "Daily Post Removal Ratio",
  "difficulty": "EASY",
  "function_name": "daily_removal_ratio",
